_2=[0,b5,[0,i,eT]],k_3="\nToggles the statics refractor on or off for the bindings at the given paths (same behavior as the editor statics toggle).\nCollapsed definitions are auto-expanded when statics end up enabled.\n\nParameters:\npaths: list(string) \xe2\x80\x94 paths to the bindings to toggle\n",k_4=[0,[0,lw,[0,S,[0,[0,b5,[0,i,j5]],[0,[0,kN,[0,S,[0,[0,lM,[0,S,[0,oKp,oKo]]],0]]],[0,[0,ic,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lM],0]]],0]]]]],0],k_5=dX,k_6=[0,cw,[0,i,bmY]],k_7=eT,k_8=[0,b5,[0,i,eT]],k_$=[0,0],k$a=[0,0],k$b=[0,1],k$c=[0,1],k$d=[0,1],k__=[0,FQ,[0,bVj,0]],k_9=[0,nA,[0,a5,[0,rL,[0,sZ,[0,mm,[0,yN,[0,BP,[0,BA,0]]]]]]]],k$l=[0,1],k$k=dm,k$j=dm,k$i=dm,k$h=m,k$g=eW,k$f="Printer.add_indent: Not_found",k$m=[0,m],k$n=[0,jE],k$p=[0,"- **checkbox** \xe2\x80\x94 Toggle UI for boolean literals."],k$q=[0,"- **slider** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (integer)."],k$r=[0,"- **sliderf** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (floating-point)."],k$s=[0,"- **card** \xe2\x80\x94 **Playing-card** editor: a tuple `(Suit, Rank)` such as `(Hearts, Ace)` or a list of those tuples. **Not** for records, modules, or `{ let \xe2\x80\xa6; \xe2\x80\xa6 }` blocks."],k$t=[0,"- **livelit** \xe2\x80\x94 Custom livelit projector for structured literal editing."],k$u=[0,"- **text** \xe2\x80\x94 Multiline string literal editor."],k$v=[0,"- **table** \xe2\x80\x94 Spreadsheet-style editor for a **list of labeled tuples** sharing the same labels; the labels become column headers. Attaches off the **elaborated** form, so it can apply where the surface syntax alone is not yet a table."],k$w=[0,"- **csv** \xe2\x80\x94 CSV **file import** UI. Attaches only when the definition is the **empty list** `[]`; after placement, import fills it with row/tuple syntax. Non-empty lists (e.g. `[1, 2, 3]`) **cannot** take this projector."],k$x=[0,"- **keybinding** \xe2\x80\x94 Key-capture editor for a string literal holding a keyboard shortcut; records the next chord pressed and commits it as the literal."],k$y=[0,"- **color** \xe2\x80\x94 Color picker for an `Oklch(l, c, h)` literal: a swatch plus lightness, chroma and hue sliders. Attaches only to that constructor applied to three float literals."],k$z=[0,0,0],k$A=[0,m,[0,"These are alternative UIs for literals and structured values that may already appear in code.",0]],k$B=[0,"### Livelits (menu projectors)",0],k$D=[0,m,0],k$E=[0,m,[0,"### Syntax projector tools (Filbert)",[0,"`place_syntax_projector(kind, paths)`, `remove_syntax_projector(paths)`, and `toggle_syntax_projector(kind, paths)` apply **syntax projector** UIs to the term selected by each path.",[0,"`kind` must be a menu projector name (`fold`, `slider`, `sliderf`, `check`, `text`, `card`, `csv`, `table`, `livelit`) \xe2\x80\x94 not `probe` or `statics` (those use the probe/statics tools).",[0,m,[0,"**CRITICAL \xe2\x80\x94 livelits are not automatic:** Ordinary Hazel code (`let speed = 50`, `let is_active = true`, list literals, records) renders as **plain text** until you call **`place_syntax_projector`**.",[0,'If the user asks how livelits work, or wants sliders/checkboxes/CSV editors/text boxes, you **must** call `place_syntax_projector` with the right `kind` on each binding path (e.g. `slider` on `"speed"`, `check` on `"is_active"`, `text` on `"message"`, `csv` only when the RHS is `[]`, `card` only on playing-card tuples/lists\xe2\x80\x94see livelit lines above; nested paths like `"config/volume"`).',[0,"**Never** describe interactive widgets as present based only on `insert_*`, `update_*`, or other edit tools \xe2\x80\x94 that is false unless the matching `place_syntax_projector` calls succeeded.",[0,m,0]]]]]]]]],k$F=iw(["## Projectors and the agent view",m,"### Fold (`\xe2\x8b\xb1`)","A **fold** is a collapsed definition in the GUI: the definition shows as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (not source text).","Use `expand` / `collapse` (see **Paths** and **View Tools** above).",m,"### Runtime probe refractor","The **probe** refractor attaches to a binding and shows evaluated values in the agent view (e.g. `expr \xe2\x89\xa1 value`).","Tools: `place_probe`, `remove_probe`, `toggle_probe`.",m,"### Statics refractor (type overlay)","The **statics** refractor shows a type ascription overlay in the GUI (offside type cell) for human clarity.","It does not change program text; the agent\xe2\x80\x99s printed context may not mirror the overlay unless printing is extended.",m]),k$G=[0,"**Projectors**: **Folds** display as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (collapsed defs; expand/collapse in the full prompt).",[0,"**Refractors** overlay bindings: **probes** show runtime values (`\xe2\x89\xa1` in context); **statics** add a type overlay in the GUI.",[0,"**Livelits** are alternate UIs for literals (checkbox, slider/sliderf, text, card, csv, table, livelit, plus fold in the menu).",[0,"**Agent tools**: `place_syntax_projector` / `remove_syntax_projector` / `toggle_syntax_projector` (see full prompt).",[0,"Full detail lives in Filbert\xe2\x80\x99s live system prompt **Projectors and the agent view** section (this excerpt may be truncated).",0]]]]],k$M=[0,m],k$L="Editor.Meta.t_of_yojson",k$K="Editor.Meta.yojson_of_t",k$J="Editor.Meta.t_of_sexp",k$H="Editor.Meta.sexp_of_t",k$T=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],k$S=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],k$U=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],k$R=[0,"Empty hole"],k$Q=hj,k$P=[0,"Missing operator"],k$N=[0,0,1],k$O=[0,0,0],k$V=[0,[0,lw,[0,S,[0,[0,b5,[0,i,j5]],[0,[0,kN,[0,S,[0,[0,lM,[0,S,[0,oKr,oKq]]],0]]],[0,[0,ic,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lM],0]]],0]]]]],0],k$W=dX,k$X=[0,cw,[0,i,bp5]],k$Y=eT,k$Z=[0,b5,[0,i,eT]],k$0=[0,[0,lw,[0,S,[0,[0,b5,[0,i,j5]],[0,[0,kN,[0,S,[0,[0,lM,[0,S,[0,oKt,oKs]]],0]]],[0,[0,ic,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lM],0]]],0]]]]],0],k$1=dX,k$2=[0,cw,[0,i,bns]],k$3=eT,k$4=[0,b5,[0,i,eT]],k$5=[0,[0,lw,[0,S,[0,[0,b5,[0,i,j5]],[0,[0,kN,[0,S,[0,[0,lM,[0,S,[0,oKv,oKu]]],0]]],[0,[0,ic,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lM],0]]],0]]]]],0],k$6=dX,k$7=[0,cw,[0,i,blK]],k$8=eT,k$9=[0,b5,[0,i,eT]],lal=[0,1],lai=[0,MF],laj=[0,dm],lak=eW,lag=[0,40],laf=[0,J2],lah=m,lae=[0,0],lab=[0,jE],lac=dm,lad=eW,k$_=boF,k$$=dOa,la